  },
  {
   "id": "note-mixers",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -790,
   "y": -494,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 300,
   "text": "**Why mix the two?** A DeltaNet layer keeps one 128×128 matrix per head (48 heads) that it updates token by token — memory and compute per token stay constant however long the context is.    \nAn attention layer stores K and V of every past token (2048 values/token/layer).    \nAt 262,144 tokens: 16 attention layers ≈ **17.2 GB** KV (bf16) vs 48 DeltaNet layers ≈ **151 MB** state (fp32)."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-rope",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 560,
   "y": -374,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 250,
   "text": "**Position**: only attention layers use RoPE — partial (64 of 256 dims), multimodal (interleaved t/h/w sections 11/11/10), θ = 1e+07. DeltaNet layers get order from their causal conv (4 taps) and recurrence.    \nContext 262,144 native; the model card gives YaRN ×4 to reach ~1M."
  },
  {
   "id": "img8",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -630,
   "y": -960,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**image / video** frames",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "patch9",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -541,
   "y": -864,
   "width": 123,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl10",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1090,
   "y": -874,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`patches [P, 1536] = 3 × 2 frames × 16²`"
  },
  {
   "id": "vit11",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -630,
   "y": -810,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**ViT ×27** (+ learned pos-embed)  \n415.9M · width 1152",
   "color": "#a78bfa"
  },
  {
   "id": "vf12",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -526,
   "y": -714,
   "width": 92,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl13",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1090,
   "y": -724,
